 "briefing": {
  "place": "Świecino by Lake Żarnowiec, Gdańsk Pomerania. 17 September 1462, the night before the battle and the whole day.",
  "story": "The Thirteen Years' War is in its ninth year. Both sides fight with hired men and neither has the money to pay them; the king pays with the silver of the Prussian towns, Gdańsk first of all. Piotr Dunin has brought the royal mercenaries and the Gdańsk men to Świecino, and the Order's hired army under Fritz Raweneck is coming against them. Stach of Łęczyca, twenty-seven, a captain of a royal company now, counts the silver for his men.",
  "goal": "Hire companies on the Gdańsk silver and set up the wagon fort with its ditch, hold the long horse fight till noon, draw the Order's horse under the Gdańsk crossbows, and take the Order's wagon fort when Raweneck falls.",
  "lose": [
   "Stach falls",
   "The Polish wagon fort is taken",
   "More than half the army runs from the field"
  ]
 },
