    {
     "do": "cutscene",
     "id": "last_reckoning",
     "at": [
      46,
      70
     ],
     "lines": [
      [
       "Chronicler",
       "The night before 17 September 1462. The Polish camp at Świecino. Fires, wagons, the clink of chains: the wagoners are chaining the wheels together. Stach sits on a wagon shaft and by the light of a candle counts the purses of silver for his company. On the next shaft sits a man in a red coat. The wagoners do not see him."
      ],
      [
       "Chronicler",
       "Eight years had passed since Chojnice. Stach served the king for pay, led his own company and, pan Jan used to say, counted money better than he prayed."
      ],
      [
       "hero_stranger",
       "Good wagons. Your grandfather learned from the Czechs to set them like this."
      ],
      [
       "hero_stach",
       "I remember you. You sat on the causeway."
      ],
      [
       "hero_stranger",
       "I did. You have a hard day tomorrow, pan captain. You have fewer men, little money, and the Order's mercenaries are angry: they are not paid either. I could help. As I helped your grandfather."
      ],
      [
       "hero_stach",
       "And the price is the same?"
      ],
      [
       "hero_stranger",
       "Your family has always paid its debts."
      ],
      [
       "hero_stach",
       "Grandfather paid."
      ],
      [
       "Chronicler",
       "A pause. The stranger looks at him for a long time, then smiles."
      ],
      [
       "hero_stranger",
       "He paid. I said myself that you owe me nothing. But I never said you need nothing."
      ],
      [
       "hero_stach",
       "What I need is for the crossbowmen not to oversleep in the morning. That I will see to myself. Go your way, pan. You are in the candle's light."
      ],
      [
       "Chronicler",
       "Stach bends over the silver again. When he raises his head, there is nobody on the next shaft."
      ],
      [
       "Chronicler",
       "Pan Jan said his father told of that night only in his old age. And added that it might have been just a sutler who wanted to sell him wine on credit. There were plenty of them in the camp."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "do": "hint",
     "text": "«The Pact» is closed in this mission: Stach has turned the stranger away. Power comes only from chapels."
    }
   ]
  },
